# Unit Tests Required

Every new feature and every bugfix must be accompanied by unit tests that cover the changed or added behavior.

## Rules

- **New feature** → add tests that verify the feature works as expected
- **Bugfix** → add a regression test that would have caught the original bug
- Tests must be placed in the appropriate test directory/file adjacent to the code under test
- Do not ship code without tests unless the user explicitly opts out

## Test placement

| Source file | Test file |
|---|---|
| `src/foo/bar.dart` | `test/foo/bar_test.dart` |
| `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/Foo.mm` | `RenderDll/XRenderMetal/test/FooTests.cpp` |

## Examples

```dart
// ❌ BAD – bugfix with no regression test
void fixedFunction() { ... }

// ✅ GOOD – bugfix accompanied by a test that would have caught the bug
void fixedFunction() { ... }

test('fixedFunction returns correct value when input is empty', () {
  expect(fixedFunction(''), equals(''));
});
```

```cpp
// ✅ GOOD – new feature with a corresponding test
TEST(FooTest, NewFeatureHandlesEdgeCase) {
    EXPECT_EQ(newFeature(0), expectedValue);
}
```
